    LLM: 'Only declare in with a hand that has three-card potential (pair or draw to straight/flush).\n\nConsider pot size versus risk of matching; going in with weak two cards risks a big loss when you receive a bad third card.\n\nIn optional second-declare variant, staying in for the third card but then dropping loses only the extra ante, not the full pot match.',
